    "body": "I picked it as an example because when a repository is sufficiently large the git status command has (in my experience, anyway) had some rather nasty performance impacts on the prompt, depending on which information you return to display. I'm not saying it's a _must_, but in my experience caching models work best with explicit keys and invalidation expectations, or they eventually grow a requirement for them.",
