    "updated_at": "2021-09-03T22:56:23Z",
    "body": "After a little thought, perhaps a little system that spawns a background task (so it doesn't impact prompt speed or performance!) that'll run version checks and compare it to the cache. This would be the best idea in my eyes. If you change rust version you'll have to regenerate the prompt at least twice as the cache would be read first, then a background task would be spawned updating the cache of need be then that'd be displayed. \n\nFeedback appreciated!\n\nPS I'm happy to implement this",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
