    "created_at": "2021-09-04T18:28:30Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-09-04T18:28:30Z",
    "body": "Whilst that would work, moving forward, an async prompt would be the way to go in my honest opinion. It would make creating a cache much easier, especially if we just use a background task because that'd how I'd see it working in my head. Literally, whenever you run the prompt it just runs the commands and compares the outputs to the one currently in the cache and the one that was just generated.\r\nHere is a little diagram I drew up:\r\n![cache](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/50248166/132104569-cb11f27e-0bca-4767-ab66-ef7bd55966a4.png)\r\n(pardon the bad drawing)\r\n\r\nA few other points I've thought of:\r\n- On old systems running Windows, the **node** version is ridiculously slow. This would fix it by making it a background job.\r\n- The Rust version check can be slow because of antivirus'. This would make it unnoticeable as it's just reading from the cache!",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/starship/starship/issues/comments/913018377/reactions",
