    "created_at": "2021-09-04T19:23:42Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-09-04T19:24:54Z",
    "body": ">  It would make creating a cache much easier, especially if we just use a background task because that'd how I'd see it working in my head.\r\n\r\nI understand it may be easier to conceptualize, but the constraint that we're working with is that our prompt needs to work across shells. As it stands, there's no easy or consistent way to implement async prompts or rerendering on all shells we support. For that reason, async is off the table.\r\n\r\nYour flow chart is identical to how a synchronous cache mechanism works, minus the background job. The worst case is that the first time the prompt is rendered for a given language, it is comparatively slow – nevertheless faster than most other similar prompts due to our concurrent implementation. Every other time it'd be instant.",
