    "created_at": "2023-12-31T08:38:26Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-12-31T08:38:26Z",
    "body": "I'd love to see some form of this. I have a use case which is potentially a variant of what's discussed in this issue, or perhaps a related but separate feature request.\r\n\r\nA custom command which generates a portion of my prompt is rather slow, but that output is expected to be constant within the same working directory. So it's acceptable to only re-run the command when I change working directories. It would be nice if the `custom` prompt segment had an easy way to take advantage of the cache. For example, a `update_if_changed = 'pwd'` which would run the `update_if_changed` command and only re-evaluate the `command` if that value changed.",
